# LF in the working tree on every platform, not just in the repository.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows clone checks every text file out as CRLF,
# and Prettier's endOfLine defaults to "lf" — so `pnpm format:check` failed on
# 73 files in a clean, correctly formatted checkout while CI passed on the same
# commit. The obvious reaction, `prettier --write`, rewrites the tree to LF,
# git hands CRLF back on the next checkout, and the check still fails.
#
# Generalises what the icon-gallery rule below already does for one file. Must
# stay ABOVE the specific rules: in .gitattributes the LAST matching pattern
# wins, so a catch-all placed later would override them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The CI job regenerates this file on Linux and fails if it differs from the
# committed copy. Without a pinned EOL it would be generated with LF and
# compared against a CRLF working copy on Windows, so the check would fail for
# a reason that has nothing to do with the icons.
packages/ui/icon-gallery.html text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are tool-generated; never merge them by hand.
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated=true

# Documentation and generated artefacts are excluded from language statistics
# so the repo language reflects the application code.
docs/** linguist-documentation=true
